# Belt to the Dockerfile's braces: COPY is already a named allowlist, but if a
# blanket copy ever sneaks in, nothing here may reach a layer. Secrets first.
#
# B-GAE-043: patterns here anchor at the CONTEXT ROOT. `__pycache__/` matched a
# top-level __pycache__ and NOTHING nested, so `COPY tests/` carried 246 of the
# laptop's .pyc files into the image with the author's home path baked into
# every one. Anything that can occur at ANY DEPTH must be written `**/…`; the
# flat form is correct only for the top-level directories at the bottom of this
# file. CI images were clean by luck alone — a fresh runner checkout has no
# caches — so this was invisible in the lane that runs most often.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
.venv/
.git/
.claude/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store
data/
docs/
plans/
ops/
PROJECT-MEMORY.md
CLAUDE.md
.run.lock
.sweep.lock
.classify.lock
.aggregator.lock
